{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-5e5f559e-5de5-4844-a95d-60111363d91c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-808a5d57fe06e2c6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-jqz94rmj/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004: Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio\n\n## Overview\n\nRHOAI must provide a default vector store available out-of-the-box so Gen AI Studio\nplayground RAG workflows keep functioning when inline providers are removed from the\nLlama Stack (OGX) distribution image (RHAISTRAT-7474). Per Staff Engineer Input, the\nselected backend is PostgreSQL with pgvector, consumed through the OGX distribution's\nexisting remote `remote::pgvector` vector_io provider. The engineering effort is\ndominated by infrastructure and provisioning of the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance, not\nby vector_io provider integration (the existing remote vector store implementation is\nlargely reusable). No custom image build, Konflux onboarding, or repo onboarding is\nneeded: the Red Hat `postgresql-16` image already includes pgvector, and the related\nimage reference is already present in the rhods-operator CSV for disconnected installs.\n\nThe central unknown is the **provisioning approach for RHOAI 3.5**, gated on the\ndelivery timing of RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization, In Progress).\nThis is resolved by an Investigation epic with three bounded outcomes, modeled as\nconditional decomposition branches. The OGX provider enablement, the Gen AI Studio BFF\nwiring, and the benchmark are invariant across outcomes and form the Tier 1\n(independent) work.\n\nAuto Rag is decoupled per Staff Engineer Input: pgvector is validated only for Gen AI\nStudio Playground RAG workflows; Auto Rag compatibility is owned by RHAISTRAT-7824.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n| E001 | Go/no-go decision: default vector store provisioning approach for RHOAI 3.5 | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| E002 | Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution | Implementation | OGX | OGX Core | P0 |\n| E003 | Wire the default pgvector vector store into Gen AI Studio playground provisioning | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| E004 | Benchmark the default vector store: inline Milvus baseline versus pgvector | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | RAG + Vector DB | P1 |\n| BRANCH-A-E005 | Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| BRANCH-B-E005 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning in the Gen AI Studio backend | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| BRANCH-C-E005 | Bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration surface for Gen AI Studio RAG | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P1 |\n\n`epic_count = 7` (4 main-plan epics + 3 conditional branch epics; branch epics are\nalternative outcomes of the same E005 provisioning slot, not additive work).\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation: provisioning go/no-go\"]\n    E002[\"E002 OGX pgvector vector_io provider enablement\"]\n    E003[\"E003 Gen AI Studio BFF default vector store wiring\"]\n    E004[\"E004 Benchmark: inline Milvus baseline vs pgvector\"]\n    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E005 Operator-based self-provisioning\"]\n    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E005 BFF-managed provisioning\"]\n    BC[\"BRANCH-C-E005 Bring-your-own PostgreSQL surface\"]\n    E002 --> E003\n    E002 --> E004\n    E001 --> BA\n    E001 --> BB\n    E001 --> BC\n```\n\nBranch epics are conditional alternatives gated by the E001 Investigation outcome;\nexactly one of BRANCH-A/B/C-E005 is selected. They are excluded from the main-plan\ncritical path. Longest main-plan chain: E002 → E003 (critical path length 2).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The BFF wiring builds against the vector_io provider configuration contract (ENABLE_PGVECTOR activation, connection parameters, secret resolution) that the OGX-side epic establishes and validates. Code builds against an API/config surface — serial. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 13 (consuming deliverable) | The benchmark measures the enabled pgvector provider path; it cannot produce results before the provider configuration is validated. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate, true gate) | The go/no-go outcome determines whether the operator-based provisioning epic exists at all (`remove` if outcome A is not selected). |\n| E001 → BRANCH-B-E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate, true gate) | The BFF-managed fallback only exists if the operator layer is not available for 3.5 and the team keeps the zero-manual-setup experience (`remove` otherwise). |\n| E001 → BRANCH-C-E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate, true gate) | The bring-your-own surface only exists if neither self-provisioning path can ship in 3.5 (`remove` otherwise). |\n| (no edge) E001 → E002 / E003 / E004 | Rule 14 / Step 5.5 Tier 1 | The provider enablement, BFF wiring (consumes a namespace PostgreSQL connection secret regardless of which path produces it), and benchmark are invariant across all three outcomes — they are the independent partial-value tier and must not be serialized behind the decision. |\n| (no edge) E003 ↔ BRANCH-A/B-E005 | Rule 15 (same repo, different areas) | The selected provisioning epic and the BFF wiring coordinate on the connection-secret contract but live in different areas (operator reconciler vs. BFF provisioning path); coordination risk, not a dependency. Main-plan epics must not depend on branch epics. |\n| (no edge) E002 ↔ E001 | Rule 14 | Provider enablement does not depend on the provisioning decision; it is required in every outcome. |\n| (no onboarding epics) | Staff Engineer Correction 2 | No custom image build, Konflux onboarding, or repo onboarding: `postgresql-16` includes pgvector, and the related image reference is already in the rhods-operator CSV. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\nThe strategy's High Level Requirements section resides in an attachment not available\nin this workspace (see Health Warnings); HLRs below are synthesized from the strategy's\nAcceptance Criteria, Success Criteria, and Staff Engineer Input.\n\n| HLR | Priority | Requirement (source) | Covering epic(s) |\n|-----|----------|----------------------|------------------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure (AC-1) | E003, BRANCH-A-E005, BRANCH-B-E005 — BRANCH-C-E005 explicitly does not satisfy this (accepted degraded fallback) |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of current capability (AC-2, scoped to Gen AI Studio per Staff Engineer Input) | E002, E003, E004 |\n| HLR-3 | P0 | Default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX/Llama Stack instance — not an inline provider (AC-4) | E002, BRANCH-A-E005, BRANCH-B-E005, BRANCH-C-E005 |\n| HLR-4 | P0 | Scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments, per-namespace isolation (AC-5) | E002, BRANCH-A-E005, BRANCH-B-E005 |\n| HLR-5 | P1 | Lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments without significant overhead (AC-6; Staff Engineer: dev-experimentation scope, order-of-magnitude, sizing per model-registry-operator reference) | E004, BRANCH-A-E005, BRANCH-B-E005 |\n| HLR-6 | P1 | Migration path from the default vector store to a production-grade vector database (open question; alignment with commonly-used vector DB providers) | E003, BRANCH-C-E005 |\n\nAC-3 (\"Auto Rag functions with the default vector store\") is removed from scope per\nStaff Engineer Input — owned by RHAISTRAT-7824 (logged below). Full coverage: every\nHLR maps to at least one main-plan epic; HLR-1's complete satisfaction additionally\nrequires exactly one of branch A or B to be selected.\n\n## Staff Engineer Override Log\n\nStaff Engineer Input takes precedence over the AI-generated technical approach. Each\noverride and its effect on the decomposition:\n\n| # | Strategy position (AI-generated) | Staff Engineer correction | Effect on decomposition |\n|---|----------------------------------|---------------------------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | OGX/LlamaStackDistribution instances require a PostgreSQL database (existing infrastructure) | OGX defaults to SQLite (`storage.kv.type`/`storage.sql.type: sqlite`); the gen-ai BFF hardcodes SQLite; PostgreSQL for vector storage is new work | Provisioning treated as new work (branch epics); ACs assert application storage remains SQLite |\n| 2 | Custom pgvector image build + pipeline onboarding (1–2 sprints estimated) | `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` includes pgvector; model-registry-operator already auto-provisions it; `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` already in the rhods-operator CSV | No image-build, `konflux-onboarding`, `repo-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics; estimate eliminated |\n| 3 | Auto Rag is an affected component with its own acceptance criteria | Decouple: validate pgvector only for Gen AI Studio Playground RAG; Auto Rag compatibility is RHAISTRAT-7824 scope | Auto Rag removed from components, ACs, and validation; HLR-2 scoped to Gen AI Studio |\n| 4 | Open questions on latency thresholds, corpus size ranges, index type | Dev-experimentation scope: no strict SLAs; sprint-1 benchmark captures inline Milvus baseline and verifies order of magnitude; flat scan sufficient for typical small document sets | Open questions removed; E004 carries order-of-magnitude ACs; no index-selection Investigation |\n| 5 | Consolidate vector and application stor