n playground deletion,\n    pod-restart handling, credential rotation; portability to the platform-shared\n    database expected in RHOAI 3.6)\n  - Bring-your-own PostgreSQL: users manually configure the OGXServer custom resource\n    spec with their connection details (aligns with the OGX 1.0 breaking changes;\n    degrades the out-of-the-box experience)\n- Record the selected approach, rationale, gate criteria, and the fallback if the\n  selected path fails late\n- Confirm the scoping model for the default vector store (per-namespace isolation is\n  the stated preference; Auto Rag is decoupled per RHAISTRAT-7824)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A decision record exists that selects exactly one provisioning approach for RHOAI\n  3.5 and states the go/no-go gate criteria and the decision date applied\n- The record documents the RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery assessment against the 3.5 timeline\n  that the decision was based on\n- The record documents the fallback approach if the selected path fails late (per\n  Staff Engineer Input: BFF-managed provisioning or bring-your-own PostgreSQL)\n- The scoping decision (per-namespace versus per-instance) is recorded, with\n  per-namespace as the default unless the assessment surfaces a concrete blocker\n- The decision is communicated to the dependent strategy removing inline providers\n  from the OGX distribution (RHAISTRAT-7474), unblocking its implementation\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box default vector store): determines which provisioning approach\n  delivers it and whether it can be fully satisfied in 3.5\n- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): confirms the per-namespace scoping model\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":87740,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa439eff7938345d","agent_id":"a452882a5395f1e83","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"f34a1b6f-a9ad-4a48-b995-da2b64e9383c","