{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f851dad7-32d3-4456-adff-6e17dcd1d150","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95b0c6826b3f7789","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-jqz94rmj/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution\n\n## Description\n\nEstablishes the OGX-distribution side of the default vector store: the remote pgvector\nvector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`, activated via the ENABLE_PGVECTOR environment\nguard) is enabled and validated for Gen AI Studio playground RAG workloads, and its\nconfiguration contract is documented for the playground provisioning layer to consume.\nThe OGX distribution already follows a provider-plugin architecture with remote-capable\nvector I/O backends (Milvus, PGVector, Qdrant), and per Staff Engineer Input the\nexisting remote vector store implementation is largely reusable — this epic is\nconfiguration and validation work, not new provider development. Vector storage is an\nindependent configuration from OGX application storage: the application storage backend\nremains on its existing SQLite default and is not touched.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify the remote pgvector vector_io provider activates correctly in the OGX\n  distribution configuration (ENABLE_PGVECTOR guard) against an external\n  pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL connection\n- Validate vector insert/query round-trips through the vector I/O API against a\n  PostgreSQL instance with the pgvector extension enabled\n- Document the configuration contract: the environment variables and connection\n  parameters required to activate the provider, and the secret-resolution behavior\n  (`_FILE`-suffixed paths for Kubernetes secret volume mounts)\n- Confirm vector data isolation semantics within the provider (vector store\n  namespaces) to support per-namespace scoping in multi-tenant environments\n- Confirm the provider operates as a remote SQL client — a separate process decoupled\n  from the OGX server, not an inline provider\n- Confirm no coupling to the OGX application storage backends: configuring only the\n  vector_io pgvector provider leaves `storage.kv.type` / `storage.sql.type` on their\n  existing SQLite defaults (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- With the pgvector provider configuration applied and a reachable pgvector-enabled\n  PostgreSQL instance, the OGX server exposes vector I/O and insert/query round-trips\n  succeed\n- The documented configuration contract activates the provider without code changes,\n  following the distribution's existing environment-variable-guarded provider\n  activation pattern\n- Configuring only the vector_io pgvector provider leaves the application storage\n  configuration unchanged from its SQLite default (verified by configuration\n  inspection/test)\n- The provider connects to PostgreSQL over the PostgreSQL protocol as a separate\n  process — no in-process or embedded vector store is involved\n- Vector store namespaces within the provider provide isolation suitable for\n  per-namespace scoping (verified by test: data written under one namespace is not\n  readable under another)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (playground RAG functions with the default vector store): provider-level\n  validation of pgvector vector I/O\n- HLR-3 (separate process, not an inline provider): remote pgvector provider decoupled\n  from the OGX instance\n- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): vector store namespace isolation semantics\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88877,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa439eff7938345d","agent_id":"a452882a5395f1e83","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"52c788eb-dfc4-4d81-8a7f-21327ee526