), keeping\n  a migration path from the default store to production-grade vector databases\n- Rollback behavior: reverting to the prior OGXServer configuration restores previous\n  behavior; vector data is re-ingested on next use, so no data migration is required\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A playground created with RAG enabled gets an OGXServer instance configured with\n  the pgvector vector_io provider pointing at the namespace PostgreSQL connection\n  secret, with no manual user configuration steps\n- Playground RAG workflows (document upload, embedding, retrieval-augmented\n  generation) function end-to-end against the default vector store with no loss of\n  current capability — a feature-parity checklist against the inline-provider\n  experience passes\n- The OGXServer application storage setting is unchanged (SQLite default) when the\n  vector store wiring is applied\n- Replacing the default vector store with an external vector database connection is\n  possible through configuration only (no code change), demonstrating the migration\n  path to production-grade vector databases\n- Disabling the default vector store configuration reverts playgrounds to prior\n  behavior without requiring data migration\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): zero-manual-step wiring for RAG-enabled playgrounds\n- HLR-2 (no loss of capability): end-to-end playground RAG parity\n- HLR-3 (separate process): provider configuration targets the remote pgvector\n  backend, never an inline provider\n- HLR-6 (migration path): configuration-only path to external vector databases\n  preserved\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88877,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa439eff7938345d","agent_id":"a452882a5395f1e83","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"a66cf26f-87fa-4264-a1a8-ab93eaeeb9fc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:31:37.737Z","subagent_type