r measurements are within the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus\n  baseline for each measured latency and throughput metric, with pass/fail stated per\n  metric\n- The report includes a resource-sizing recommendation for the default\n  PostgreSQL/pgvector instance derived from measured consumption and the\n  model-registry-operator reference sizing\n- Any measured deviation beyond an order of magnitude is documented with a follow-up\n  recommendation (index selection or sizing change) for the implementing team\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (no loss of capability): order-of-magnitude performance comparison against\n  the inline Milvus baseline\n- HLR-5 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments): resource consumption\n  measurement and sizing recommendation\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88877,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa439eff7938345d","agent_id":"a452882a5395f1e83","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"50e55462-f0bc-4b42-b962-580b52cdfde7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:31:44.013Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
