{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cdd8154f-5ea3-4660-9c38-8d2e4ce05032","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5d423f6b8af4777","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-jqz94rmj/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E005.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n\n## Description\n\nActivated when the go/no-go decision selects operator-based self-provisioning — the\noutcome where the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time for\nRHOAI 3.5 and provides the RHOAI-controlled operator layer. The operator self-provisions\nthe default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance for Gen AI Studio, following the\nmodel-registry-operator's auto-provisioned PostgreSQL pattern (per-instance Deployment,\nService, credential Secret, and persistent storage). No custom image build or pipeline\nonboarding is required: the Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image includes pgvector out of the\nbox, and the related-image environment variable is already present in the rhods-operator\nCSV for disconnected installs. When the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL\n(DSC-managed) becomes available in RHOAI 3.6, consumers can switch to the shared\nconnection string.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector instance provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator\n  layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization: Deployment, Service,\n  credential Secret, and persistent storage, per playground namespace\n- Use the Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included), resolving the image\n  reference through the related-image environment variable already present in the\n  rhods-operator CSV (disconnected-install compatible)\n- Apply resource requests/limits referencing the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL\n  sizing as the starting point, adjustable per benchmark results\n- Provision one instance per playground namespace (per-namespace isolation for\n  multi-tenant environments)\n- Produce the PostgreSQL connection secret in the playground namespace conforming to\n  the consumption contract used by the Gen AI Studio playground vector store wiring\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL (RHOAI 3.6+) is\n  available, the consumer can switch to the shared connection string instead of the\n  self-provisioned instance\n- Owner-operator lifecycle: cleanup of the provisioned instance and its data when the\n  playground is deleted\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Creating a RAG-enabled playground in a namespace results in a running\n  pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance provisioned by the operator, with no manual user\n  steps\n- The provisioned instance exposes a connection secret in the playground namespace\n  matching the documented consumption contract\n- Deleting the playground cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL instance and its\n  persistent data (verified by test)\n- Resource requests/limits applied to the provisioned instance match the documented\n  sizing reference, with any deviations recorded\n- The provisioned image reference resolves via the related-image environment variable\n  rather than a hardcoded registry path (disconnected-install compatible)\n- Vector data in one namespace is not visible from another namespace's instance\n  (per-namespace isolation verified by test)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): operator self-provisioning with zero manual steps\n- HLR-3 (separate process): PostgreSQL runs as its own deployment, decoupled from the\n  OGX server instance\n- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): one instance per namespace with isolated data\n- HLR-5 (lightweight): sizing per the model-registry-operator reference\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":91195,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa439eff7938