 behavior on BFF restart and PostgreSQL pod restart (no orphaned or\n  duplicated instances), and a credential-rotation approach\n- Design for portability: behind a configuration switch, consume an externally\n  provided connection string (platform-shared database, RHOAI 3.6+) instead of\n  self-provisioning\n- Produce the connection secret conforming to the consumption contract used by the\n  Gen AI Studio playground vector store wiring\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Configuring a playground with RAG in a namespace without a suitable existing\n  PostgreSQL instance results in the BFF creating a running pgvector-enabled instance\n  and its connection secret, with no manual user steps\n- Deleting the playground triggers cleanup of the BFF-provisioned PostgreSQL resources\n  (Deployment, Service, PVC, Secret) — verified by test\n- BFF restart and PostgreSQL pod restart are handled without orphaned or duplicated\n  instances — verified by test\n- The self-provisioning path is behind a configuration switch that allows consuming\n  an externally provided connection string instead (portability to the platform-shared\n  database)\n- Resource requests/limits on the created instance match the documented sizing\n  reference, with any deviations recorded\n- Vector data in one namespace is not visible from another namespace's instance\n  (per-namespace isolation verified by test)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): BFF self-provisioning with zero manual steps\n- HLR-3 (separate process): PostgreSQL runs as its own deployment, decoupled from the\n  OGX server instance\n- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): one instance per namespace with isolated data\n- HLR-5 (lightweight): sizing per the model-registry-operator reference\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":91195,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa439eff7938345d","agent_id":"a452882a5395f1e83","session_id"