through the configuration surface,\n  and a RAG-enabled playground uses it as its vector store with no code changes\n- Documentation states the pgvector prerequisite, the supported PostgreSQL versions,\n  and the steps to configure the connection\n- Release notes state that RAG capabilities require a user-provided PostgreSQL in this\n  release (manual setup), with the default provisioned vector store referenced as the\n  planned follow-up\n- The same configuration surface accepts connections to external vector databases,\n  demonstrating the migration path from the default store\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (migration path to production-grade vector databases): the bring-your-own\n  surface is the configuration path to external databases\n- HLR-3 (separate process): the user-provided PostgreSQL is decoupled from the OGX\n  server instance\n- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): partial by design — this branch explicitly does not deliver\n  the out-of-the-box experience; the limitation is an accepted outcome of the go/no-go\n  decision\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":91195,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa439eff7938345d","agent_id":"a452882a5395f1e83","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"40eea76f-fe9f-446d-a1b7-e7d5d4707293","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:32:10.202Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
