{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82cded9914f9c941","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Go/no-go decision: default vector store provisioning approach for RHOAI 3.5'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Go/no-go decision: default vector store provisioning approach for RHOAI 3.5\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the central unknown of this strategy: which provisioning approach ships the\n30\tdefault PostgreSQL/pgvector vector store for Gen AI Studio in RHOAI 3.5. Operator-based\n31\tself-provisioning requires a RHOAI-controlled operator layer, which is delivered by the\n32\tdashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress) — a hard dependency\n33\twhose delivery timing relative to the 3.5 release is not yet known. Until that is\n34\tresolved, the provisioning approach cannot be fixed. This investigation produces a\n35\tdecision record that selects one of three bounded outcomes and defines the go/no-go\n36\tgate criteria, per Staff Engineer Input directing the development team to define this\n37\tgate as part of sprint planning. The decision determines which conditional branch of\n38\tthe decomposition is activated; the OGX provider work, the Gen AI Studio wiring, and\n39\tthe benchmark proceed independently of it.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Assess the delivery status and timeline of RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator\n44\t  modularization) against the RHOAI 3.5 release plan\n45\t- Define the go/no-go gate criteria and decision date for the provisioning approach\n46\t- Assess viability of each candidate approach:\n47\t  - Operator-based self-provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator, following the\n48\t    model-registry-operator's auto-provisioned PostgreSQL pattern (requires the\n49\t    modularized operator layer)\n50\t  - BFF-managed provisioning in the gen-ai backend, mirroring the existing guardrails\n51\t    infrastructure provisioning (lifecycle caveats: cleanup on playground deletion,\n52\t    pod-restart handling, credential rotation; portability to the platform-shared\n53\t    database expected in RHOAI 3.6)\n54\t  - Bring-your-own PostgreSQL: users manually configure the OGXServer custom resource\n55\t    spec with their connection details (aligns with the OGX 1.0 breaking changes;\n56\t    degrades the out-of-the-box experience)\n57\t- Record the selected approach, rationale, gate criteria, and the fallback if the\n58\t  selected path fails late\n59\t- Confirm the scoping model for the default vector store (per-namespace isolation is\n60\t  the stated preference; Auto Rag is decoupled per RHAISTRAT-7824)\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- A decision record exists that selects exactly one provisioning approach for RHOAI\n65\t  3.5 and states the go/no-go gate criteria and the decision date applied\n66\t- The record documents the RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery assessment against the 3.5 timeline\n67\t  that the decision was based on\n68\t- The record documents the fallback approach if the selected path fails late (per\n69\t  Staff Engineer Input: BFF-managed provisioning or bring-your-own PostgreSQL)\n70\t- The scoping decision (per-namespace versus per-instance) is recorded, with\n71\t  per-namespace as the default unless the assessment surfaces a concrete blocker\n72\t- The decision is communicated to the dependent strategy removing inline providers\n73\t  from the OGX distribution (RHAISTRAT-7474), unblocking its implementation\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box default vector store): determines which provisioning approach\n78\t  delivers it and whether it can be fully satisfied in 3.5\n79\t- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): confirms the per-namespace scoping model\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3b99b53c4dda3f","agent_id":"a97702bc5ac309863","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"ba7e9b49-42cd-4b58-ab70-43ce29e802c9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:35:08.263Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82cded9914f9c941","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
