{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa27f985e4a011ab","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: OGX Core\n6\tteam: OGX\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tEstablishes the OGX-distribution side of the default vector store: the remote pgvector\n34\tvector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`, activated via the ENABLE_PGVECTOR environment\n35\tguard) is enabled and validated for Gen AI Studio playground RAG workloads, and its\n36\tconfiguration contract is documented for the playground provisioning layer to consume.\n37\tThe OGX distribution already follows a provider-plugin architecture with remote-capable\n38\tvector I/O backends (Milvus, PGVector, Qdrant), and per Staff Engineer Input the\n39\texisting remote vector store implementation is largely reusable — this epic is\n40\tconfiguration and validation work, not new provider development. Vector storage is an\n41\tindependent configuration from OGX application storage: the application storage backend\n42\tremains on its existing SQLite default and is not touched.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Verify the remote pgvector vector_io provider activates correctly in the OGX\n47\t  distribution configuration (ENABLE_PGVECTOR guard) against an external\n48\t  pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL connection\n49\t- Validate vector insert/query round-trips through the vector I/O API against a\n50\t  PostgreSQL instance with the pgvector extension enabled\n51\t- Document the configuration contract: the environment variables and connection\n52\t  parameters required to activate the provider, and the secret-resolution behavior\n53\t  (`_FILE`-suffixed paths for Kubernetes secret volume mounts)\n54\t- Confirm vector data isolation semantics within the provider (vector store\n55\t  namespaces) to support per-namespace scoping in multi-tenant environments\n56\t- Confirm the provider operates as a remote SQL client — a separate process decoupled\n57\t  from the OGX server, not an inline provider\n58\t- Confirm no coupling to the OGX application storage backends: configuring only the\n59\t  vector_io pgvector provider leaves `storage.kv.type` / `storage.sql.type` on their\n60\t  existing SQLite defaults (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope)\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- With the pgvector provider configuration applied and a reachable pgvector-enabled\n65\t  PostgreSQL instance, the OGX server exposes vector I/O and insert/query round-trips\n66\t  succeed\n67\t- The documented configuration contract activates the provider without code changes,\n68\t  following the distribution's existing environment-variable-guarded provider\n69\t  activation pattern\n70\t- Configuring only the vector_io pgvector provider leaves the application storage\n71\t  configuration unchanged from its SQLite default (verified by configuration\n72\t  inspection/test)\n73\t- The provider connects to PostgreSQL over the PostgreSQL protocol as a separate\n74\t  process — no in-process or embedded vector store is involved\n75\t- Vector store namespaces within the provider provide isolation suitable for\n76\t  per-namespace scoping (verified by test: data written under one namespace is not\n77\t  readable under another)\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- HLR-2 (playground RAG functions with the default vector store): provider-level\n82\t  validation of pgvector vector I/O\n83\t- HLR-3 (separate process, not an inline provider): remote pgvector provider decoupled\n84\t  from the OGX instance\n85\t- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): vector store namespace isolation semantics\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3b99b53c4dda3f","agent_id":"a97702bc5ac309863","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"002617c6-fabd-457b-aebd-9763ce434632","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:35:08.851Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa27f985e4a011ab","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
