{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4bfb82c4fc5c9c3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Wire the default pgvector vector store into Gen AI Studio playground provisioning\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Wire the default pgvector vector store into Gen AI Studio playground provisioning\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tExtends the Gen AI Studio backend (gen-ai BFF) so that playgrounds created with RAG\n35\tcapabilities are configured to use the remote pgvector vector_io provider, consuming a\n36\tPostgreSQL connection secret available in the playground namespace. Today the BFF\n37\tcreates OGXServer instances for the playground with application storage hardcoded to\n38\tSQLite; this epic adds the vector_io configuration on the same creation path. The\n39\twiring is approach-invariant: the connection secret may be produced by operator-based\n40\tself-provisioning, by BFF-managed provisioning, or supplied by the user\n41\t(bring-your-own) — the consumption contract is identical, so this work proceeds\n42\tregardless of which provisioning approach is selected for RHOAI 3.5. Users perform no\n43\tmanual setup for RAG workflows when a default provisioned instance is available.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer creation path (llamastack_config.go) to configure\n48\t  the pgvector vector_io provider (ENABLE_PGVECTOR plus connection parameters) for\n49\t  RAG-enabled playgrounds\n50\t- Define and consume the PostgreSQL connection-secret contract in the playground\n51\t  namespace (secret name and keys), resolving credentials via the OGX `_FILE`\n52\t  secret-resolution pattern\n53\t- Preserve the existing application storage configuration (SQLite) on created\n54\t  OGXServer instances — only the vector_io configuration changes\n55\t- Preserve the configuration path to external vector databases (remote\n56\t  Milvus/Qdrant/PGVector providers remain selectable through configuration), keeping\n57\t  a migration path from the default store to production-grade vector databases\n58\t- Rollback behavior: reverting to the prior OGXServer configuration restores previous\n59\t  behavior; vector data is re-ingested on next use, so no data migration is required\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A playground created with RAG enabled gets an OGXServer instance configured with\n64\t  the pgvector vector_io provider pointing at the namespace PostgreSQL connection\n65\t  secret, with no manual user configuration steps\n66\t- Playground RAG workflows (document upload, embedding, retrieval-augmented\n67\t  generation) function end-to-end against the default vector store with no loss of\n68\t  current capability — a feature-parity checklist against the inline-provider\n69\t  experience passes\n70\t- The OGXServer application storage setting is unchanged (SQLite default) when the\n71\t  vector store wiring is applied\n72\t- Replacing the default vector store with an external vector database connection is\n73\t  possible through configuration only (no code change), demonstrating the migration\n74\t  path to production-grade vector databases\n75\t- Disabling the default vector store configuration reverts playgrounds to prior\n76\t  behavior without requiring data migration\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): zero-manual-step wiring for RAG-enabled playgrounds\n81\t- HLR-2 (no loss of capability): end-to-end playground RAG parity\n82\t- HLR-3 (separate process): provider configuration targets the remote pgvector\n83\t  backend, never an inline provider\n84\t- HLR-6 (migration path): configuration-only path to external vector databases\n85\t  preserved\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3b99b53c4dda3f","agent_id":"a97702bc5ac309863","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"1ec45113-c560-4d2c-ac52-94ba63de03a5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:35:11.468Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4bfb82c4fc5c9c3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
