{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b323012b8c7950fa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E004\n3\ttitle: 'Benchmark the default vector store: inline Milvus baseline versus pgvector'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: RAG + Vector DB\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 0\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Benchmark the default vector store: inline Milvus baseline versus pgvector\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tCaptures the performance baseline of the inline Milvus provider (the capability being\n35\treplaced when inline providers are removed from the OGX distribution) and verifies\n36\tthat pgvector is in the same order of magnitude on representative playground RAG\n37\tworkloads. Per Staff Engineer Input this is dev-experimentation scope: strict latency\n38\tSLAs are not required, typical playground RAG usage involves small document sets, and\n39\ta flat scan (no index) is sufficient for the default instance. The epic also validates\n40\tPostgreSQL resource sizing for the provisioned default instance, using the\n41\tmodel-registry-operator's PostgreSQL requests/limits as the starting point.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Define representative playground RAG workloads (small document sets; flat scan, no\n46\t  vector index) for measurement\n47\t- Capture the inline Milvus provider baseline on those workloads (latency and\n48\t  throughput)\n49\t- Measure pgvector-backed vector I/O on the same workloads through the OGX vector I/O\n50\t  API\n51\t- Record resource consumption (CPU/memory) of the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance under\n52\t  those workloads\n53\t- Compare measured consumption against the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL\n54\t  resource requests/limits as the sizing starting point and recommend adjustments\n55\t- Publish a benchmark report with results, pass/fail per metric, and the sizing\n56\t  recommendation\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A benchmark report exists covering both the inline Milvus baseline and the pgvector\n61\t  measurements on identical representative workloads\n62\t- pgvector measurements are within the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus\n63\t  baseline for each measured latency and throughput metric, with pass/fail stated per\n64\t  metric\n65\t- The report includes a resource-sizing recommendation for the default\n66\t  PostgreSQL/pgvector instance derived from measured consumption and the\n67\t  model-registry-operator reference sizing\n68\t- Any measured deviation beyond an order of magnitude is documented with a follow-up\n69\t  recommendation (index selection or sizing change) for the implementing team\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-2 (no loss of capability): order-of-magnitude performance comparison against\n74\t  the inline Milvus baseline\n75\t- HLR-5 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments): resource consumption\n76\t  measurement and sizing recommendation\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3b99b53c4dda3f","agent_id":"a97702bc5ac309863","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"ed968dcb-bb8d-48c4-bf88-374384ea595b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:35:12.202Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b323012b8c7950fa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
