{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af19dc423e6c15a1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E005\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n16\t    not land in time for RHOAI 3.5, this epic is removed and the go/no-go decision\n17\t    falls back to BFF-managed provisioning or the bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration\n18\t    surface.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tActivated when the go/no-go decision selects operator-based self-provisioning — the\n40\toutcome where the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time for\n41\tRHOAI 3.5 and provides the RHOAI-controlled operator layer. The operator self-provisions\n42\tthe default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance for Gen AI Studio, following the\n43\tmodel-registry-operator's auto-provisioned PostgreSQL pattern (per-instance Deployment,\n44\tService, credential Secret, and persistent storage). No custom image build or pipeline\n45\tonboarding is required: the Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image includes pgvector out of the\n46\tbox, and the related-image environment variable is already present in the rhods-operator\n47\tCSV for disconnected installs. When the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL\n48\t(DSC-managed) becomes available in RHOAI 3.6, consumers can switch to the shared\n49\tconnection string.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector instance provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator\n54\t  layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization: Deployment, Service,\n55\t  credential Secret, and persistent storage, per playground namespace\n56\t- Use the Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included), resolving the image\n57\t  reference through the related-image environment variable already present in the\n58\t  rhods-operator CSV (disconnected-install compatible)\n59\t- Apply resource requests/limits referencing the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL\n60\t  sizing as the starting point, adjustable per benchmark results\n61\t- Provision one instance per playground namespace (per-namespace isolation for\n62\t  multi-tenant environments)\n63\t- Produce the PostgreSQL connection secret in the playground namespace conforming to\n64\t  the consumption contract used by the Gen AI Studio playground vector store wiring\n65\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL (RHOAI 3.6+) is\n66\t  available, the consumer can switch to the shared connection string instead of the\n67\t  self-provisioned instance\n68\t- Owner-operator lifecycle: cleanup of the provisioned instance and its data when the\n69\t  playground is deleted\n70\t\n71\t## Acceptance Criteria\n72\t\n73\t- Creating a RAG-enabled playground in a namespace results in a running\n74\t  pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance provisioned by the operator, with no manual user\n75\t  steps\n76\t- The provisioned instance exposes a connection secret in the playground namespace\n77\t  matching the documented consumption contract\n78\t- Deleting the playground cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL instance and its\n79\t  persistent data (verified by test)\n80\t- Resource requests/limits applied to the provisioned instance match the documented\n81\t  sizing reference, with any deviations recorded\n82\t- The provisioned image reference resolves via the related-image environment variable\n83\t  rather than a hardcoded registry path (disconnected-install compatible)\n84\t- Vector data in one namespace is not visible from another namespace's instance\n85\t  (per-namespace isolation verified by test)\n86\t\n87\t## HLR Traceability\n88\t\n89\t- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): operator self-provisioning with zero manual steps\n90\t- HLR-3 (separate process): PostgreSQL runs as its own deployment, decoupled from the\n91\t  OGX server instance\n92\t- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): one instance per namespace with isolated data\n93\t- HLR-5 (lightweight): sizing per the model-registry-operator reference\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3b99b53c4dda3f","agent_id":"a97702bc5ac309863","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"3831e959-f3ae-4106-882a-1bf6c828fe8e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:35:15.461Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af19dc423e6c15a1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
