{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaddc523bd3cf2c6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E005\n3\ttitle: BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning in the Gen AI Studio backend\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the go/no-go decision does not select BFF-managed provisioning,\n16\t    this epic is removed; the selected alternative is operator-based self-provisioning\n17\t    (if the operator layer lands) or the bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration surface.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning in the Gen AI Studio backend\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tActivated when the go/no-go decision selects the BFF-managed fallback — the operator\n39\tlayer is not available for RHOAI 3.5 and the team keeps the zero-manual-setup\n40\texperience. The gen-ai BFF provisions the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance directly,\n41\tmirroring how it currently provisions guardrails infrastructure: creating the\n42\tPostgreSQL Deployment, Service, PVC, and credential Secret when a playground with RAG\n43\tis configured and no suitable instance exists in the namespace. Per Staff Engineer\n44\tInput, two design concerns need explicit attention: the BFF is not an operator with a\n45\treconciliation loop (cleanup on playground deletion, pod-restart handling, and\n46\tcredential rotation need explicit design), and the implementation must be portable —\n47\twhen the platform-provided shared database becomes available (RHOAI 3.6+), the BFF\n48\tshould consume the shared connection string rather than self-provision.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Implement BFF-managed creation of the pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL Deployment,\n53\t  Service, PVC, and credential Secret when a RAG-enabled playground is configured and\n54\t  no suitable instance exists in the namespace\n55\t- Use the Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included), resolving the image\n56\t  reference through the related-image environment variable for disconnected installs\n57\t- Apply resource requests/limits per the model-registry-operator PostgreSQL sizing\n58\t  reference, adjustable per benchmark results\n59\t- Design lifecycle handling without a reconciliation loop: cleanup on playground\n60\t  deletion, behavior on BFF restart and PostgreSQL pod restart (no orphaned or\n61\t  duplicated instances), and a credential-rotation approach\n62\t- Design for portability: behind a configuration switch, consume an externally\n63\t  provided connection string (platform-shared database, RHOAI 3.6+) instead of\n64\t  self-provisioning\n65\t- Produce the connection secret conforming to the consumption contract used by the\n66\t  Gen AI Studio playground vector store wiring\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- Configuring a playground with RAG in a namespace without a suitable existing\n71\t  PostgreSQL instance results in the BFF creating a running pgvector-enabled instance\n72\t  and its connection secret, with no manual user steps\n73\t- Deleting the playground triggers cleanup of the BFF-provisioned PostgreSQL resources\n74\t  (Deployment, Service, PVC, Secret) — verified by test\n75\t- BFF restart and PostgreSQL pod restart are handled without orphaned or duplicated\n76\t  instances — verified by test\n77\t- The self-provisioning path is behind a configuration switch that allows consuming\n78\t  an externally provided connection string instead (portability to the platform-shared\n79\t  database)\n80\t- Resource requests/limits on the created instance match the documented sizing\n81\t  reference, with any deviations recorded\n82\t- Vector data in one namespace is not visible from another namespace's instance\n83\t  (per-namespace isolation verified by test)\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability\n86\t\n87\t- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): BFF self-provisioning with zero manual steps\n88\t- HLR-3 (separate process): PostgreSQL runs as its own deployment, decoupled from the\n89\t  OGX server instance\n90\t- HLR-4 (multi-tenant scoping): one instance per namespace with isolated data\n91\t- HLR-5 (lightweight): sizing per the model-registry-operator reference\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3b99b53c4dda3f","agent_id":"a97702bc5ac309863","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"b40c8cd6-66bd-462d-956e-1344240fc409","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:35:16.152Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaddc523bd3cf2c6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
