{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa0770a8d522280a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E005\n3\ttitle: Bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration surface for Gen AI Studio RAG\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If either self-provisioning path ships in RHOAI 3.5, this epic\n16\t    is removed and the out-of-the-box experience is preserved; the configuration surface\n17\t    it builds remains relevant only as the migration path to external vector databases.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration surface for Gen AI Studio RAG\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tActivated when the go/no-go decision selects the degraded fallback — neither\n39\toperator-based nor BFF-managed self-provisioning can ship in RHOAI 3.5. Customers\n40\tbring their own PostgreSQL for RAG capabilities in the playground, manually configuring\n41\tthe OGXServer custom resource spec with their PostgreSQL connection details (an\n42\texplicit connection-string secret). This aligns with the breaking changes introduced in\n43\tOGX 1.0, even though the playground largely abstracts OGX from users. This outcome does\n44\tnot satisfy the out-of-the-box acceptance criterion — the manual-setup limitation is a\n45\tconsciously accepted decision recorded in the go/no-go decision record and must be\n46\trelease-noted. The same configuration surface is also the migration path from the\n47\tdefault vector store to production-grade external vector databases.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Expose configuration for a user-provided PostgreSQL connection (connection-string\n52\t  secret) on the playground/OGXServer configuration surface\n53\t- Document the pgvector extension prerequisite on the user-provided PostgreSQL\n54\t  instance and the supported PostgreSQL versions (Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 and later\n55\t  include pgvector)\n56\t- Keep the playground abstraction intact: users configure a database connection, not\n57\t  OGX internals\n58\t- Record the accepted limitation (manual setup required for RAG in this release) in\n59\t  user-facing release notes, referencing the planned default provisioned vector store\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A user can supply a PostgreSQL connection secret through the configuration surface,\n64\t  and a RAG-enabled playground uses it as its vector store with no code changes\n65\t- Documentation states the pgvector prerequisite, the supported PostgreSQL versions,\n66\t  and the steps to configure the connection\n67\t- Release notes state that RAG capabilities require a user-provided PostgreSQL in this\n68\t  release (manual setup), with the default provisioned vector store referenced as the\n69\t  planned follow-up\n70\t- The same configuration surface accepts connections to external vector databases,\n71\t  demonstrating the migration path from the default store\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-6 (migration path to production-grade vector databases): the bring-your-own\n76\t  surface is the configuration path to external databases\n77\t- HLR-3 (separate process): the user-provided PostgreSQL is decoupled from the OGX\n78\t  server instance\n79\t- HLR-1 (out-of-the-box): partial by design — this branch explicitly does not deliver\n80\t  the out-of-the-box experience; the limitation is an accepted outcome of the go/no-go\n81\t  decision\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa3b99b53c4dda3f","agent_id":"a97702bc5ac309863","session_id":"738b0e56-7748-46a7-9251-8b7683e92d2f","uuid":"3f7eb7c1-9f4d-4653-9b3b-c480c797c533","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:35:17.021Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa0770a8d522280a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
