{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad4451f848e8f0a5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-8004\n10\t\n11\t## Review Summary\n12\t\n13\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n14\tRecommendation: accept\n15\t\n16\tcontract validator: OK (`python3 skills/epic-decompose/scripts/validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-8004` exited 0 — epic body sections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last, priority inheritance, implementation-type parallelism, and shared-surface enforcement all pass). Triage: absent (full decomposition), so the 7-epic output (4 main-plan epics + 3 mutually exclusive conditional branches) is the expected shape; no triage contradiction.\n17\t\n18\t## Criterion Details\n19\t\n20\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n21\t\n22\tAll six synthesized HLRs map to at least one epic, and every P0 HLR (HLR-1 through HLR-4) is covered by main-plan epics: HLR-1 → E003 + branches A/B (branch C's descope is explicit and release-noted per Health Warning 3), HLR-2 → E002/E003/E004, HLR-3 → E002 + all branches, HLR-4 → E002 + branches A/B. P1 HLRs are covered, not silently deferred: HLR-5 → E004 + sizing ACs on branches A/B; HLR-6 → E003 + BRANCH-C-E005 with the handling rationale in a self-contained note (Health Warning 5), satisfying the bundling-recording check.\n23\t\n24\tPriority inheritance is correct: E001/E002 are P0 with no deps; E003 (P0) depends on E002 (P0); E004 (P1) and branch C (P1) depend only on P0 epics and block no P0 work — confirmed by enumerating every epic's `dependencies` list. E004's P1 despite the Blocker-priority strategy is justified in Health Warning 2 (Staff Engineer relaxed it to dev-experimentation scope; nothing depends on it). No priority collapse: E003's P1 HLR-6 bundling is tightly coupled to the same config surface (a config-only path preserved by not