it from the Gen AI Studio work; E004 is attributed to RAG + Vector DB. All three components (Gen AI Studio, OGX Core, RAG + Vector DB) are in the canonical `.context/rhai-components.txt` list. No epic is oversized — each is a single focused deliverable well under the ~2-week guideline (E002 is configuration + validation; E003 extends one code path; E004 is a benchmark harness + report; each branch is one provisioning mechanism).\n37\t\n38\tNo heterogeneous monolith, no standalone enforcement-tool epic, no work-product type mixing (BRANCH-C's documentation/release-note ACs document its own configuration surface, not curated content authoring). No scope duplication: E003 (consumer of the connection secret) and BRANCH-B-E005 (producer of the PostgreSQL instance + secret) are complementary halves of one contract split along the conditional boundary — the wiring is invariant across outcomes while provisioning is not, which is the correct split axis; the coordination risk is documented (Health Warning 6). BRANCH-C vs E003's migration-path AC is incidental overlap (preserving an existing OGX config-selectable capability), and branches are mutually exclusive alternatives, not siblings in one plan.\n39\t\n40\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n41\t\n42\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its go/no-go outcome determines which of three branch epics exists (each with `gate_failure_impact.action: remove`), so it changes downstream structure. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (validated provider config + documented contract, BFF code, benchmark report, provisioning code/config surface). Gating metadata is complete and correct: every branch has both `action` and a populated `fallback_approach`; no main-plan epic depends on an Investigation without `gated_by`; every `gated_by` target (E001) appears in that epic's direct `dependencies`. No epic has `gated_by` without `gate_failure_impact`. Signal fields are type-appropriate throughout (investigation_signals on E001, ai_signals on all Implementation epics).\n43\t\n44\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n45\t\n46\tE001's five investigation signals match the rubric conditions: `question_specificity: 1` (three named approaches, defined pass/fail), `source_accessibility: 0` (correctly scored down — the gating fact, RHAISTRAT-7164's landing timing, does not yet exist in any readable artifact), `local_runnability: 1` (Go binary + embedded PostgreSQL), `cluster_hardware_dependence: -1` (only peripheral as-deployed verification needs a cluster), `human_judgment_required: -2` (the gating question is itself a sprint-planning human decision, per Staff Engineer Input).\n47\t\n48\tImplementation signal values are consistent with the rubric and the strategy content: E004's 0s for pattern_precedent/adapter_pattern/existing_foundation are correct for a greenfield benchmark harness; BRANCH-A's `existing_foundation: 0`, `external_dependency: -1` (hard RHAISTRAT-7164 dependency) are correct; E003's `open_questions: 0` is the right middle given the co-designed secret contract and directionally-resolved scoping model. `architecture_claims: 1` on all six Implementation epics is calibrated: each rationale names a context file, and I verified the citations against `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/` — ogx-distribution.md corroborates PGVector as a remote SQL client on 5432/TCP, the stripping of inline providers (docling, faiss, milvus-inline), and `_FILE` secret resolution; odh-dashboard.md corroborates the gen-ai BFF federated Go sidecar with K8s CRUD; model-registry-operator.md corroborates the controller-created postgres Deployments; ogx-k8s-operator.md corroborates the OGXServer CR (ogx.io/v1beta1). No arithmetic checked (pipeline-computed).\n49\t\n50\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n51\t\n52\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs: E003 (the replacement of inline-provider-backed behavior) carries rollback ACs (\"Disabling the d